<% content_for :title, "Reporting and Protection | SafeSpace Malaysia" %>

<section class="page-hero page-hero--mint">
  <div class="container page-hero__content">
    <span class="eyebrow">Reporting and protection</span>
    <h1>Know your options before you decide.</h1>
    <p>You can seek medical care, specialist support or safety planning whether or not you are ready to make a police report.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="protection-orders">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">Malaysian legal framework</span>
      <h2>Domestic Violence Act 1994 (Act 521)</h2>
      <p>The Act provides protection measures for domestic violence and works alongside the Penal Code. Eligibility depends on the relationship and circumstances of the case.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="definition-grid">
      <article><span>EPO</span><h3>Emergency Protection Order</h3><p>An authorised JKM welfare officer issues an EPO. It is valid for seven days from issue and takes effect when served. A police report is not required to apply.</p></article>
      <article><span>IPO</span><h3>Interim Protection Order</h3><p>The court issues an IPO while police investigate a domestic violence case. Police and JKM can assist with an application.</p></article>
      <article><span>PO</span><h3>Protection Order</h3><p>The court issues a PO in connection with criminal proceedings involving domestic violence. Ask JKM or a specialist service about the applicable process.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="source-links">Source: <a href="https://www.jkm.gov.my/portalassets/jkm/documents/garis-panduan-pengendalian-kes-keganasan-rumah-tangga.pdf">KPWKM / JKM domestic violence case guidelines, 2023</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">Possible next steps</span>
      <h2>Where you can go</h2>
      <p>In an emergency, call 999. Otherwise, choose the service that meets your immediate needs.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="steps">
      <article><span class="steps__number">1</span><div><h3>Police station</h3><p>You may make a report in Bahasa Malaysia or English at any police station. Ask for a copy of the report and keep it somewhere safe.</p></div></article>
      <article><span class="steps__number">2</span><div><h3>Government hospital</h3><p>One Stop Crisis Centres in government hospital emergency departments provide treatment and can document injuries. Medical treatment does not require a police report.</p></div></article>
      <article><span class="steps__number">3</span><div><h3>Social Welfare Department</h3><p>Contact JKM or Talian Kasih to ask about welfare assistance, shelter referrals and available protection measures.</p></div></article>
      <article><span class="steps__number">4</span><div><h3>Specialist organisation</h3><p>A survivor-support organisation can explain options, help with safety planning and accompany you through next steps where available.</p></div></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint">
  <div class="container split-panel split-panel--top">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">If it is safe</span>
      <h2>Information you may want to keep</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Dates, times and a brief description of incidents.</li>
        <li>Photos of injuries or damaged belongings.</li>
        <li>Threatening messages, emails, recordings or screenshots.</li>
        <li>Names and contact information of witnesses.</li>
        <li>Medical documents and copies of previous reports.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="fine-print">Only collect or store evidence when it is safe. Your immediate safety matters more than documentation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="next-step-card">
      <span class="eyebrow">Prepare for a visit</span>
      <h3>Consider bringing</h3>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Your identification, if accessible</li>
        <li>A trusted person for support</li>
        <li>Medication and essential items</li>
        <li>Important phone numbers</li>
      </ul>
      <%= link_to "Find support contacts", hotline_path, class: "button button--primary" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--compact">
  <div class="container disclaimer-card">
    <strong>Important</strong>
    <p>This page provides general educational information, not legal advice. Procedures can vary, so a specialist service can help you understand options for your circumstances.</p>
  </div>
</section>
